Subject: [PATCH] ssdk: mp: enable 50 MHz output for a forced 2.5G link

The Archer AX55 connects the IPQ5018 UNIPHY to an RTL8367S switch and
requires its 50 MHz reference clock output. The upstream PCS description
sets UNIPHY_CLK_REF to 50 MHz; the NSS tree configures the same link through
SSDK's forced-speed property instead. Handle 2500 Mbps alongside the
existing 1000 Mbps case so the reference clock is explicitly enabled.

--- a/src/adpt/mp/adpt_mp_uniphy.c
+++ b/src/adpt/mp/adpt_mp_uniphy.c
@@ -286,6 +286,10 @@ _adpt_mp_uniphy_clk_output_set(a_uint32_t
 	{
 		_adpt_mp_uniphy_clk_output_ctrl_set(dev_id, index, UNIPHY_CLK_RATE_25M);
 	}
+	else if ((force_port) && (force_speed == FAL_SPEED_2500))
+	{
+		_adpt_mp_uniphy_clk_output_ctrl_set(dev_id, index, UNIPHY_CLK_RATE_50M);
+	}
 	phy_id = hsl_port_phyid_get(dev_id, SSDK_PHYSICAL_PORT2);
 	if (phy_id == QCA8030_PHY || phy_id == QCA8033_PHY || phy_id == QCA8035_PHY)
 	{
